From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:42:10 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 24/37] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: describe the GPU on J714c,
 J873s, K114s, K116c

These four boards inherit the inventory GPU node from t6050-peripherals.dtsi,
compatible "apple,agx-t6050". Neither drm/asahi (which matches "gpu,t6050"
and "apple,agx-g17s") nor the loader's GPU handoff (which looks for
"apple,agx-g17s", or "apple,agx-g17c" under /soc@2300000000) accepts it, so
the GPU never binds on them.

Describe the GPU as on the booted boards of the same part:
 - J714c and K116c (M5 Max): t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi, as J716c, on its own
   /soc@2300000000 bus (T6050_GPU_BUS). J714c already runs its PMP, so its
   GPU stays on the PMP's GFX report entry as before.
 - J873s and K114s (M5 Pro): t6050-gpu-g17s.dtsi, as K116s and J714s.

Nothing here is per board: the driver picks its configuration from the GPU's
ID registers, the loader fills the reservations and operating points from
the ADT the Mac boots with and checks the firmware build before it enables
anything. Everything stays disabled until it does, so a loader that refuses
leaves these boards as they are now.

No other board's DTB changes. Not yet booted on any of the four.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714c.dts | 5 ++++-
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j873s.dts | 3 +++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114s.dts | 2 ++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k116c.dts | 4 ++++
 4 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

